making use of next() 


const express=require("express");
const app=express();


//route handler 
// if we send the empty route handler ,it will  keep on sending
// you will not get the response back ,there will be time out hit 
///user is the route 
// it will execute the code line by line 
//as Javascript is syronochous ,it will give line by line 
//if there is no first response,then it will move to the second route handler 
//if we put next on the first route then we can move to the next route handler 

// code will run line by line  for the first route  handler and second route handler 



